  "reading": "All four channels agree on every period. That is four instruments, but only ONE of them is not a program reading a render (C-112): the agreement of three OCR passes is not three independent witnesses. The pixel read is what makes the OCR readings evidence rather than output. What this does NOT establish: that the publisher's two sentences mean what the plan's E9 wants them to mean, and that p.6's pair is the only aggregate in the document (it is not -- see C-112/C-113). On the C-112 disagreement itself: the per-category tab row carries a THIRD quantity, not the bullet (C-121) -- it equals effective in 01-02, high_value in 03/06/07/08/11 and NEITHER in 04 and 10. 2025-04's bullet reads 3,999 while 6663 sits in that tab row, so 6663 is another element, not a second reading of the bullet. See results/63_E9_query_labels.json.",
